      "math_academy_id": "e-385",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\csc{x}(\\csc{x}+3\\cot{x} )\\, \\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\csc^2 x \\, \\textrm dx = -\\cot x + C\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\int \\csc x \\cot x \\, \\textrm dx = -\\csc x + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
